164-Debugging priority rule:
165-- address the highest-risk or most blocking failure surface first
166-- prefer the cheapest meaningful probe that can falsify the leading cause
167:- if ambiguity remains high under a tight budget, narrow scope or switch to propose-only instead of broad speculative editing
168:- when the reported defect is a stale sentence, owner statement, or other file-local wording defect in a runtime/control document, treat the report as a target hypothesis for the smallest likely owner file first
169:- confirm the local owner file and adjacent ownership statements before widening the search surface
170:- if the local confirmation remains weak, keep the patch narrow or switch to propose-only instead of broadening the edit set
