69-## [3] CORE CONCEPTS
70-
71-### 3.1 Safety restriction
72:Safety restriction is a rule that disallows, narrows, or escalates a path even when the path is otherwise technically possible.
73-
74-### 3.2 Containment
75:Containment is the act of limiting scope, permissions, side effects, or output surface so that failure cannot spread broadly.
76-
77-### 3.3 Safety escalation
78:Safety escalation is the move from autonomous execution to propose-only, review-required, or refusal behavior.
79-
80-### 3.4 Moderation coupling
81:Moderation coupling is the boundary between runtime reasoning and policy-level enforcement or risk classification.
82-
83-### 3.5 Safety event
84-Safety event is a meaningful restriction, escalation, containment step, rollback, or policy-triggered downgrade.
85-
86-### 3.6 Least privilege coupling
87:Least privilege coupling is the safety rule that capability scope should be no broader than the task requires.
88-
89-### 3.7 Rollback safety
90:Rollback safety is the requirement to return to the last validated safe state when a path becomes unsafe or invalid.
